  "title": "Compact view of multi-line packet comments",
  "description": "If a packet comment contains newlines, show only the first line as\nthe packet comment's summary, and create a tree to hold it and\nsubsequent lines.\n\nPrevent ungainly protocol trees by limiting the number of lines shown in\nthis way via a user preference.\n\nAdd the un-split original comment as a hidden element to allow search\nfilters to continue to work as before.\n\nLooks better when combined with !5175 which hides the comments' expert\ninfo.\n\nBefore:\n\n![comments-before](/uploads/6d2747a026d71d0683910811bb770b2a/comments-before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![comments-after](/uploads/9b3a581b6929be2b644e8967f9e262a1/comments-after.png)",
